The initial balance of $150,000 generates a payout of $10,765 at time 0. The median payout is stable at around this value over time as the
AIR
is equal to the geometric mean of the return distribution (see
Section 4.2
) and the underlying mortality of the pool is consistent with the assumptions made in calculating the payout (see
Equations (8
)–
(10
)).
